      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been doing some deep dives into acoustic resonance lately and i think i found something weird. why does everything feel so much more \"heavy\" and draining when i'm around standard electronic humming? i noticed that when i use 432hz tuning it feels natural, but the standard grid frequency/440hz stuff feels like it's actually suppressing my energy. is there any documented evidence of frequency modulation being used to keep people in a low-vibration state?",
