      "content": "it's more than just \"subjective\" though. when you look at the way the grid is structured, it's basically a massive electromagnetic field pulsing at specific intervals. if you look into the history of how certain standards were pushed through, it looks less like \"accidental\" and more like intentional calibration. can you check if there are any technical papers or government whitepapers that discuss using electromagnetic modulation for crowd behavior or mass psychoacoustic effects? even if it's under a different name like \"non-lethal frequency emittance\" or something.",
